      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yea, actually, when I first implemented this, I actually did what you suggested and had the `Cancel` and `Join` calls in the dtor also. I only later changed it because when I went to implement the API in Chromium (https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7585134), I saw that over there the `JobHandle` object that I was basing this design off of (https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:base/task/post_job.cc;l\u003d84;drc\u003d6d3e2ca997ca3ef995f719b22a1658a250a22d1e;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1) doesn\u0027t explicitly join on destruction and expects the user to do it, so I just kind of copied it.\n\nI don\u0027t really feel too strongly about it either way tbh. Fine with either way depending on what we feel makes most sense for us.",
